{
  "name": "Build a lead list of local businesses in any city into Google Sheets with SpecStream",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Build a lead list of every local business in a city\n\nType a trade and a city into the form. The workflow asks SpecStream for every match from the live web (maps, directories, each business's own site) and writes the rows to Google Sheets: name, website, phone, and the page each row came from.\n\nA Maps search stops at about 120 places. This keeps going until it has the number you asked for, up to 10,000.\n\n### How it works\n1. The form collects the trade, the city, an optional condition and your maximum price.\n2. SpecStream reads the request and quotes the most it can cost. Nothing is spent yet.\n3. If the quote is at or below your maximum, the workflow approves it. If not, it stops and tells you the price.\n4. It checks every 30 seconds until the run ends, then writes one row per business to your sheet.\n\n### Set up (5 minutes)\n1. Get a free API key at [specstream.ai](https://specstream.ai) under **Agents & API**. New accounts get $10 of credit, no card.\n2. In n8n, create a **Bearer Auth** credential with the key and pick it in the five SpecStream HTTP nodes.\n3. Connect Google Sheets and choose an empty sheet in **Add rows to your sheet**. The first run writes the headers.\n4. Open the form URL from **Describe the list** and submit it.\n\n### Price\n5¢ a business for a plain list with phone and website, 15¢ when it has to meet a condition such as a rating. The workflow approves a quote only when it is at or below your maximum. You pay for the matches, and a run that finds nothing is free.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 540
      },
      "id": "21b8cd92-e56e-5d88-8452-c84870654fd7",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Describe the list\nThe form builds one plain sentence, for example: *HVAC companies in Columbus, Ohio, with their phone number and website*. Add a condition such as *rated 4.5 or better with fewer than 20 Google reviews* to narrow it.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "bd50bf7c-599c-5651-b71e-2ac974e650ee",
      "name": "Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Read the request and price it\nReading and pricing are free. **Get the price** returns the most this list can cost; **Within your maximum?** stops the run if the price is above what you typed.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 940,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "ddc74c9a-8414-51b3-8329-a98d3eb8d65d",
      "name": "Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Approve, then wait for the list\n**Approve and start** is the only step that spends. It reuses one key per execution, so a retry never buys the list twice. The loop checks progress every 30 seconds; most lists finish in 2 to 10 minutes.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 1000,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "18fdc41b-2c80-55c0-a0e1-79d61dcbc0fc",
      "name": "Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1400,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 4. Into your sheet\nOne row per business. **Source** is the page the row came from and **List** opens the full list in SpecStream, where you can keep it current or send it to a CRM.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "4eacb6ec-c193-527f-ab5e-3a657321c9ef",
      "name": "Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2420,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
